WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.579 --> 00:00:19.740
Somehow I managed to knock the gunman to the floor again, and Holmes escaped his clutches.

2
00:00:20.641 --> 00:00:25.462
The stranger squirmed mightily, but I held onto him while Holmes blew a whistle out the window.

3
00:00:26.262 --> 00:00:30.583
In a moment two policemen and Inspector Lestrade burst into the house and came to our rescue.

4
00:00:31.383 --> 00:00:35.737
Holmes and his old friend exchanged greetings, while the two policemen pulled their prisoner upright.

5
00:00:35.757 --> 00:00:37.538
"You fiend!"

6
00:00:37.938 --> 00:00:38.718
he shouted at Holmes.

7
00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:41.299
"You clever, clever fiend!"

8
00:00:42.099 --> 00:00:45.301
Holmes picked up one of the policemen's lanterns and illuminated the man's face.

9
00:00:45.321 --> 00:00:52.184
"Gentlemen," Holmes said, "may I introduce Colonel Sebastian Moran, one of the best shots that our army has

10
00:00:52.324 --> 00:00:52.964
ever produced."

11
00:00:53.784 --> 00:00:59.026
The fierce old man said nothing, but glared at Holmes with a strange mixture of hatred and amazement.

12
00:01:01.107 --> 00:01:02.688
Holmes calmly looked him up and down.

13
00:01:03.456 --> 00:01:07.499
"Colonel, I haven't had the pleasure of seeing you since you were paying such close attention to me

14
00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:08.580
at the Reichenbach Falls."

15
00:01:09.561 --> 00:01:13.865
Snarling with rage, Moran sprang forward, but the policemen kept him from attacking Holmes.

16
00:01:13.885 --> 00:01:19.069
"I never imagined that you'd make use of this conveniently empty house," Holmes went on.

17
00:01:19.089 --> 00:01:23.753
"I thought you'd attack me from the street, where Inspector Lestrade and his men were waiting.

18
00:01:24.794 --> 00:01:27.076
Aside from that, everything has gone as I expected."

19
00:01:27.956 --> 00:01:29.518
Colonel Moran turned to Lestrade.

20
00:01:29.538 --> 00:01:32.000
"There's no reason I have to listen to this man.

21
00:01:32.852 --> 00:01:34.753
If you're going to arrest me, then take me away."

22
00:01:34.773 --> 00:01:39.116
"Oh, don't worry, we're going to arrest you Lestrade paused dramatically.

23
00:01:39.136 --> 00:01:41.397
"For the attempted murder of Mr.

24
00:01:41.477 --> 00:01:42.258
Sherlock Holmes."

25
00:01:42.278 --> 00:01:46.100
"No, no, that's not the right charge!"

26
00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.541
Holmes was busy examining Moran's gun.

27
00:01:48.561 --> 00:01:51.883
"Lestrade, I don't think you realize who you're arresting.

28
00:01:52.664 --> 00:01:55.566
This is the man the whole London police force has been searching for.

29
00:01:56.346 --> 00:01:59.208
You need to charge Colonel Moran with the murder of Ronald Adair."

30
00:02:00.044 --> 00:02:02.986
Lestrade drew in a sharp breath and stared at the man before us.

31
00:02:03.967 --> 00:02:05.228
"Ronald Adair's killer!

32
00:02:06.089 --> 00:02:08.211
But how did he manage that on a street full of people?"

33
00:02:08.991 --> 00:02:13.495
Holmes explained that Moran had used an air gun to shoot Adair through the open window of his

34
00:02:13.535 --> 00:02:17.738
study. "I've been aware of air guns for years, but never actually encountered one."

35
00:02:18.699 --> 00:02:20.180
Holmes handed the weapon to Lestrade.

36
00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:24.584
"They're tremendously powerful yet relatively quiet when compared to other guns."

37
00:02:24.604 --> 00:02:30.504
"So that's how the colonel was able to fire the gun without anyone noticing," Lestrade said.

38
00:02:31.505 --> 00:02:32.185
Holmes nodded.

39
00:02:32.205 --> 00:02:38.069
"And now, Watson, if you can endure the draft from a broken window, let's retire to my rooms

40
00:02:38.109 --> 00:02:38.909
to talk things over."

41
00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:42.951
I was delighted to see that Holmes' rooms were just as I remembered them.

42
00:02:43.852 --> 00:02:45.392
There were two occupants—Mrs.

43
00:02:45.412 --> 00:02:50.455
Hudson, who beamed at us both, and the wax dummy, which had played such an important role in

44
00:02:50.475 --> 00:02:51.416
the evening's adventure.

45
00:02:52.336 --> 00:02:55.978
It stood on a small table with one of Holmes' old dressing gowns draped around it.

46
00:02:55.998 --> 00:03:00.657
"Mrs. Hudson, I hope you followed my instructions," Holmes said to his landlady.

47
00:03:00.677 --> 00:03:02.778
"Yes," she replied.

48
00:03:02.798 --> 00:03:07.982
"I always approached the dummy on my knees, so that my shadow wouldn't appear on the blind."

49
00:03:08.002 --> 00:03:13.505
"Excellent!" Holmes rubbed his hands together with satisfaction.

50
00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:15.467
"Did you see where the bullet went?"

51
00:03:16.347 --> 00:03:21.271
Mrs. Hudson handed him the bullet, which had passed through the dummy, bounced off a wall, and landed

52
00:03:21.311 --> 00:03:21.771
on the rug.

53
00:03:22.732 --> 00:03:27.075
Holmes threw off his shabby coat and put on his dressing gown, which he took from the dummy.

54
00:03:27.095 --> 00:03:31.398
"And now, Watson, sit in your chair, and we'll discuss this case."

55
00:03:32.499 --> 00:03:35.722
Holmes beckoned to the seat where I'd spent many happy hours, and Mrs.

56
00:03:35.762 --> 00:03:36.903
Hudson left to make tea.

57
00:03:36.923 --> 00:03:41.267
"You'll be surprised to learn that Colonel Moran had a distinguished career in the army."

58
00:03:41.747 --> 00:03:44.670
Holmes had no idea what had motivated Moran's turn to crime.

59
00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:50.234
But by the time he had retired from the army and arrived in London, Professor Moriarty was aware

60
00:03:50.295 --> 00:03:50.915
of his talents.

61
00:03:52.877 --> 00:03:56.140
Eventually Moran became the criminal mastermind's chief of staff.

62
00:03:57.004 --> 00:04:02.066
Professor Moriarty kept the colonel supplied with money and only used him for high-stakes jobs that an ordinary

63
00:04:02.126 --> 00:04:03.106
criminal couldn't handle.

64
00:04:04.086 --> 00:04:08.488
When Moriarty's gang was broken up, there was no evidence to connect Moran with the professor.

65
00:04:08.508 --> 00:04:12.729
"Do you remember when I visited you, and I closed the shutters for fear of an air gun?"

66
00:04:13.169 --> 00:04:13.769
Holmes asked.

67
00:04:14.609 --> 00:04:16.910
I admitted that I thought it was rather strange at the time.

68
00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:21.572
"I knew that if anyone had an air gun, it would be Colonel Moran, one of the best

69
00:04:21.692 --> 00:04:22.452
shots in the world.

70
00:04:23.404 --> 00:04:28.027
When we were in Switzerland, he followed us with Moriarty, and he's undoubtedly the man who threw rocks

71
00:04:28.087 --> 00:04:28.347
at me."

72
00:04:30.668 --> 00:04:33.310
As long as the colonel was free, Holmes would be in danger.

73
00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:37.772
But Holmes couldn't kill Moran because then he would be on trial for murder.

74
00:04:37.792 --> 00:04:43.055
"All I could do was read the crime reports in the newspapers and hope that he'd reveal himself."

75
00:04:43.075 --> 00:04:47.858
"And then came the murder of Ronald Adair Holmes nodded.

76
00:04:47.878 --> 00:04:53.593
"It sounded like Colonel Moran's type of crime: a wealthy member of society mysteriously killed by what I

77
00:04:53.653 --> 00:04:54.933
suspected was an air gun."

78
00:04:55.833 --> 00:05:00.315
When Holmes returned to London, he was instantly spotted by Moran's lookout, who alerted the colonel.

79
00:05:00.335 --> 00:05:04.396
"Colonel Moran couldn't fail to connect my sudden return with his crime."

80
00:05:05.376 --> 00:05:06.036
Holmes laughed.

81
00:05:07.097 --> 00:05:08.777
"He must have been terribly alarmed."

82
00:05:09.777 --> 00:05:13.419
Holmes knew that Moran would immediately try to kill him, probably with an air gun.

83
00:05:15.439 --> 00:05:18.040
So he placed the bust in the window and alerted the police.

84
00:05:19.056 --> 00:05:22.719
"Those were the men you so cleverly spotted in the doorway," Holmes said to me.

85
00:05:22.739 --> 00:05:26.062
"I can understand why Moran was after you," I said.

86
00:05:26.082 --> 00:05:28.945
"But what was his motive for murdering Adair?"

87
00:05:29.926 --> 00:05:34.530
Holmes explained that Moran and Adair had recently won a lot of money playing whist together.

88
00:05:35.570 --> 00:05:38.533
On the day of the murder, Adair discovered that Moran had been cheating.

89
00:05:39.394 --> 00:05:44.578
Adair probably threatened to reveal what Moran had done unless he immediately resigned from his card clubs and

90
00:05:44.638 --> 00:05:46.240
promised never to play cards again.

91
00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:50.581
"But exclusion from his clubs would mean financial ruin," Holmes said.

92
00:05:50.601 --> 00:05:54.322
"Since Moriarty's death, he'd had to find another source of income."

93
00:05:54.342 --> 00:05:58.884
"And he lived on the money he made by winning at cards!"

94
00:05:59.464 --> 00:05:59.844
I said.

95
00:05:59.864 --> 00:06:01.725
"So he murdered Adair."

96
00:06:01.745 --> 00:06:03.886
"Exactly," Holmes said.

97
00:06:03.906 --> 00:06:07.307
"Adair didn't want to profit from his whist partner's cheating.

98
00:06:08.207 --> 00:06:11.168
That night he was figuring out what he owed his fellow card players.

99
00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:15.762
Adair had locked the door because he didn't want his mother or sister to come in and ask

100
00:06:15.782 --> 00:06:17.363
what he was doing with all that money.

101
00:06:18.224 --> 00:06:22.006
Meanwhile Moran had found another convenient hiding place and fired his gun."

102
00:06:22.026 --> 00:06:26.568
"Well, Holmes, once again you've solved the case," I said as Mrs.

103
00:06:26.608 --> 00:06:27.769
Hudson brought us some tea.

104
00:06:27.789 --> 00:06:32.551
"And may I say, on behalf of the entire city of London, that we are all delighted to

105
00:06:32.591 --> 00:06:33.372
have you back!"
